.\" Manual page for healthchecks-systemd-oneshot.
.TH HEALTHCHECKS\-SYSTEMD\-ONESHOT 1 2026-10-27 healthchecks-helpers 1.0
.SH NAME
healthchecks\-systemd\-oneshot \- ping Healthchecks.io from a systemd oneshot service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B healthchecks\-systemd\-oneshot
.RB [ \-jvh ]
.I URL
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B healthchecks\-systemd\-oneshot
reports the outcome of a systemd oneshot service to
.UR https://healthchecks.io
Healthchecks.io
.UE .
.PP
It is intended to be invoked from
.B ExecStartPost=
(to signal the start of the run) and
.B ExecStopPost=
(to signal success or failure).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-j
For
.B ExecStopPost=
attach the service's journal entries.
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose logging.
.TP
.B \-h
Print usage.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SERVICE_RESULT
Set by systemd for
.BR ExecStopPost= ;
its presence distinguishes the final ping from the start ping.
.TP
.B EXIT_CODE
When
.BR exited ,
the run is reported with
.BR EXIT_STATUS .
.TP
.B EXIT_STATUS
Process exit status; must parse as a number in 0\(en255.
.TP
.B INVOCATION_ID
Used to build the
.B rid=
parameter and to match journal entries for
.BR \-j .
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status is the libcurl result code:
.B 0
on success, non-zero otherwise (e.g.\&
.B 7
couldn't connect,
.B 22
HTTP response >= 400 because
.B CURLOPT_FAILONERROR
is set).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Start and result pings for a oneshot service:
.PP
.nf
[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/bin/myjob
ExecStartPost=healthchecks-systemd-oneshot https://hc-ping.com/<uuid>
ExecStopPost=healthchecks-systemd-oneshot -j https://hc-ping.com/<uuid>
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://healthchecks.io/docs/http_api/
Healthchecks.io HTTP API
.UE ,
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR systemd.exec (5)
